Q: I have a method that calls “console.log”, and I invoke it inside a “console.log” call. Why do I get an extra “undefined” in the output? A: <p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function Person(fname, lname) {
 this.fname = fname,
 this.lname = lname,
 this.getName = function(){
  console.log(`${fname} ${lname}`)
 }
}
var x1 = new Person("amnah", "khatun")
var x2 = new Person("xyz", "pqr")
console.log(x1.getName())</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: delay applying styles in nextjs with tailwind A: <p>Tried wrapping custom styles in <code>@layer</code> ?</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@import &quot;tailwindcss&quot;;

@layer components {
  .card {
    background-color: #fff;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Or you can just use inline tailwindcss:</p>
<pre class="lang-tsx prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class=&quot;bg-white text-gray-500&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: CSS Transition between 2 icons (Material Design) A: <p>The newer <a href="https://fonts.google.com/icons" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Google Material Symbols</a> library supports variable fonts. That means you can use the <code>font-variation-settings</code> property to modify the same icon by, for example, changing if the icon is filled or not.</p>
<p>The <code>font-variation-settings</code> can be animated to make it a smooth transition.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const star = document.querySelector('#star');

star.addEventListener('click', () =&gt; {
  star.classList.toggle('is-filled');
});</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.material-symbols-outlined {
  font-size: 48px !important;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: font-variation-settings 0.2s ease-in-out;

  font-variation-settings:
    'FILL' 0, /* Without fill */
    'wght' 400,
    'GRAD' 0,
    'opsz' 24;
}

.material-symbols-outlined.is-filled {
  font-variation-settings:
    'FILL' 1, /* With fill */
    'wght' 400,
    'GRAD' 0,
    'opsz' 24;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined:opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@20..48,100..700,0..1,-50..200&amp;icon_names=star" /&gt;

&lt;span id="star" class="material-symbols-outlined"&gt;
star
&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
